WEBVTT

00:01.240 --> 00:05.870
<i>Before a hero was born in Ente Isla...</i>

00:07.470 --> 00:11.640
<i>Crimson blood blanketed the soil 
in the wake of constant massacre.</i>

00:15.450 --> 00:21.950
<i>The demon realm had no unifying 
ruler after the ancient king died.</i>

00:22.430 --> 00:26.990
<i>It was a lawless world 
governed by fear and violence.</i>

00:28.310 --> 00:34.110
If you ask me, though, "paradise" is 
the most suspicious word in the lexicon.

00:34.110 --> 00:38.640
I actually find the red here quite beautiful.

00:42.480 --> 00:45.900
But red is... scary...

00:45.900 --> 00:49.380
So you're not afraid 
of the color you see now?

00:49.960 --> 00:52.410
Would you like to know its name?

00:55.400 --> 00:57.960
That means learning about the world.

00:58.980 --> 01:03.790
It also means learning a new side 
of the red you're so afraid of.

01:08.360 --> 01:10.210
What's your name?

01:10.810 --> 01:12.050
Satan.

01:12.460 --> 01:13.960
A good name.

01:14.510 --> 01:18.330
I'm about to give you knowledge 
that will help you learn of the world.

01:18.830 --> 01:23.460
Knowledge to help you find 
this fear-clouded red beautiful.

01:30.110 --> 01:32.770
The color you saw is called...

01:33.980 --> 01:38.910
m 370 218 l 609 218 609 245 370 245

01:34.490 --> 01:36.490
A-Amazing!

01:35.610 --> 01:38.910
<b>The Devil Returns to the Workplace</b>

01:35.610 --> 01:38.910
<b>The Devil Returns to the Workplace</b>

01:36.880 --> 01:38.910
The faucets are automatic!

01:38.910 --> 01:42.190
And we have state-of-the-art 
tankless toilets!

01:42.190 --> 01:44.510
It'll be so easy to clean behind them!

01:44.510 --> 01:46.380
And what's more...

01:47.620 --> 01:50.020
The lid has a motion sensor!

01:50.020 --> 01:52.550
Sounds like you're focused on the bathroom,

01:52.550 --> 01:54.370
but be sure to check out 
the rest of the place, okay?

01:54.370 --> 01:55.760
Of course, ma'am!

01:56.060 --> 01:59.760
The booths are in calm colors and 
designed to evoke expensive leather.

02:00.130 --> 02:03.640
And the furnishings have 
a similar simple, calm tone.

02:03.910 --> 02:06.550
The new burger griddles are the latest model,

02:06.550 --> 02:09.020
and we've got three instead of two.

02:09.020 --> 02:13.050
And for the pièce de résistance...

02:13.050 --> 02:15.780
A café space on the second floor: the MgCafé!

02:18.760 --> 02:22.830
It's like it's not MgR's! In a good way!

02:22.830 --> 02:25.070
Like, the space is more refined,

02:25.070 --> 02:27.290
but it still has that relaxed
MgRonald's feel!

02:27.290 --> 02:30.220
No fair seeing it without me!

02:30.220 --> 02:32.850
I don't even have a shift assigned yet.

02:32.850 --> 02:38.170
Sire, what is the difference between 
this "MgCafé" and regular MgRonald's?

02:38.170 --> 02:42.120
Well, like you'd expect from the name, 
it's got more types of coffee.

02:42.120 --> 02:45.650
You can get stuff like café au lait, 
caffè latte, and espresso.

02:46.200 --> 02:50.230
And we're sellin' more café-style foods 
like hot dogs and cakes!

02:50.230 --> 02:54.690
I forget, what's the difference 
between café au lait and caffè latte?

02:55.060 --> 02:57.150
Um, well, you know...

02:57.150 --> 03:02.950
Café au lait has milk in it, 
and caffè latte has milk... uh...

03:03.370 --> 03:05.720
Basically they're both coffee milk.

03:05.720 --> 03:07.120
"Coffee milk"?!

03:07.120 --> 03:10.910
That phrase almost ruins 
the entire "café" vibe...

03:12.290 --> 03:13.860
Ugh, Urushihara!

03:13.860 --> 03:16.990
How many times have I told you to make 
more tea if you finish the pitcher?!

03:16.990 --> 03:20.070
Lay off. There's still some left.

03:20.910 --> 03:22.760
Oh, Häagen-Desse.

03:23.090 --> 03:27.840
That was a gift from Miss Sasaki! 
At least thank her first!

03:27.840 --> 03:31.600
And rinse out the container 
before you throw it away!

03:31.600 --> 03:33.870
Otherwise we'll get more Blattella germa—

03:33.870 --> 03:39.240
I see the two demon generals are 
bickering about small stuff, as usual.

03:39.240 --> 03:42.110
At least knock, Emi.

03:42.480 --> 03:45.030
Chi-sis! Papa!

03:45.390 --> 03:47.280
Alas Ramus!

03:47.280 --> 03:49.620
We're borrowing Chiho for a while.

03:49.620 --> 03:51.210
What do you mean "borrow"?

03:51.210 --> 03:54.910
Didn't you spirit her off 
somewhere yesterday, too?

03:54.910 --> 03:57.420
We're having a girls' talk. 
Don't worry about it.

03:58.060 --> 04:00.990
You guys watch TV with 
Alas Ramus or something.

04:00.990 --> 04:02.190
Papa!

04:02.190 --> 04:05.930
Hi, Alas Ramus! Chi and the others 
have to go somewhere,

04:05.930 --> 04:07.300
so you and I will hang out.

04:17.730 --> 04:22.110
<b>Okorinbo Shogun</b>

04:22.110 --> 04:25.490
Are you sure Mr. Maou isn't suspicious?

04:25.490 --> 04:28.010
Alas Ramus has him distracted.

04:28.010 --> 04:30.800
I'd rather not use her like this, but...

04:30.800 --> 04:35.370
Of the two of them, the one we really 
need to watch out for is Alciel.

04:35.790 --> 04:37.380
<i>I'll make you pay!</i>

04:37.380 --> 04:39.170
Angry Bo!

04:39.170 --> 04:41.380
Yup, he's angry.

04:41.770 --> 04:44.680
Doesn't this strike you as odd, Sire?

04:44.680 --> 04:46.550
Huh? What's odd?

04:46.550 --> 04:50.890
The three of them having 
a girls' talk two days in a row.

04:51.190 --> 04:52.780
What's wrong with that?

04:53.110 --> 04:56.900
Means we get more time with Alas Ramus.

04:57.270 --> 05:00.520
Is "girls' talk" really what they're doing?

05:11.590 --> 05:15.780
Are you kidding me? Emilia will kill you 
if she finds out you eavesdropped.

05:18.540 --> 05:19.750
What is it?

05:19.750 --> 05:22.460
They're watching <i>Okorinbo</i>, too.

05:22.460 --> 05:24.800
Girls' talk with a samurai soundtrack?

05:24.800 --> 05:27.550
Quiet! They're saying something.

05:28.140 --> 05:31.060
Blood... bath... only choice...

05:31.060 --> 05:34.060
"Bloodbath"? Who are they fighting?!

05:34.060 --> 05:38.560
I doubt we'll be able to 
keep them in the dark forever.

05:35.110 --> 05:37.080
<i>I'll make you two pay!</i>

05:38.560 --> 05:41.440
We ought to come up with 
a cover story now, and—

05:41.950 --> 05:47.360
In the dark... cover story? 
What are they discussing?

05:47.360 --> 05:49.950
Know anything about it, Alas Ramus?

05:49.950 --> 05:53.120
<i>I'll punish you!</i>

05:49.950 --> 05:53.120
I pun-ish you!

05:56.570 --> 05:57.980
They seem to be going out.

05:57.980 --> 06:00.960
Probably to chat at 
a restaurant or something.

06:00.960 --> 06:06.340
Chi wouldn't betray us. 
Let's let them do their thing.

06:06.690 --> 06:08.420
I'll tail them.

06:10.230 --> 06:11.850
Hey, Ashiya!

06:11.850 --> 06:13.850
Eh, let him do his thing.

06:20.100 --> 06:23.110
What are they carrying?

06:32.440 --> 06:33.820
They gave me the slip!

06:37.750 --> 06:39.250
<b>Public Telephone</b>

06:41.060 --> 06:42.350
Hello?

06:42.740 --> 06:45.410
<i>Hello, is this Miss Suzuki's phone?</i>

06:45.410 --> 06:47.210
M-M-Mister Ashiya!

06:47.210 --> 06:50.010
Wh-What has you calling at this hour?

06:50.010 --> 06:54.630
<i>I'd like to ask you something, 
if you don't mind.</i>

06:54.630 --> 06:57.540
O-Of course! Ask m-me anything.

06:58.600 --> 06:59.800
No luck.

07:00.270 --> 07:03.430
They gave me the slip, 
and then I called Miss Suzuki

07:03.430 --> 07:07.840
to ask her if Emilia has been 
acting strange recently,

07:07.840 --> 07:10.420
but I didn't obtain any useful information.

07:10.420 --> 07:13.040
Tailing them was going a bit far.

07:13.040 --> 07:14.910
Yes, Sire, but...

07:15.570 --> 07:19.910
Plus, I bet you got poor 
Rika Suzuki's hopes up...

07:20.280 --> 07:24.170
It's my fault for expecting anything good.

07:24.650 --> 07:27.170
Alas Ramus, we're back!

07:27.760 --> 07:29.500
Huh? Where's Chi?

07:29.500 --> 07:30.670
Her place.

07:31.090 --> 07:33.940
I walked her home. Don't worry.

07:33.940 --> 07:35.220
Mama!

07:35.220 --> 07:38.050
Have you been a good girl, Alas Ramus?

07:38.050 --> 07:40.430
I watched Angry Bo with Papa.

07:40.430 --> 07:42.770
Where were you?

07:42.770 --> 07:43.790
Around.

07:43.790 --> 07:46.370
You could've just had your 
girls' talk in Bel's room.

07:46.370 --> 07:48.450
It's drab here.

07:48.450 --> 07:52.910
We found a swanky new pasta 
place that was really good.

07:52.910 --> 07:54.080
Why, you!

07:54.080 --> 07:57.330
Is your goal to lord your 
richer lifestyle over us?!

07:57.330 --> 08:00.630
Did you know our dinner 
would be discount cabbage

08:00.630 --> 08:03.830
and "last chance" chopped pork 
at less than one yen a gram,

08:03.830 --> 08:06.180
with naught but salt and 
pepper per seasoning?!

08:06.180 --> 08:08.590
Are you rubbing it in our faces?!

08:08.590 --> 08:12.340
Not another word, Ashiya. You'll depress me.

08:12.340 --> 08:15.950
No way is there a swanky 
pasta place in Sasazuka.

08:15.950 --> 08:20.350
That's insulting! Apologize to 
Sasazuka for underestimating it!

08:24.320 --> 08:28.200
What's Emilia's endgame here?

08:28.200 --> 08:33.190
Probably nothing beyond 
taking her mind off things.

08:33.190 --> 08:34.610
What things?

08:35.190 --> 08:39.870
Maybe Emi's having a tough time 
shaking off what happened.

08:40.220 --> 08:43.640
Emilia's dad is alive out there somewhere.

08:43.640 --> 08:45.650
All I did was tell her so.

08:45.650 --> 08:48.390
So she's escaping into girls' talk 
with Chiho Sasaki and Bel

08:48.390 --> 08:52.680
because she's lost sight 
of her goal to take you down?

08:52.680 --> 08:55.460
Dunno if it's <i>that</i> serious, but yeah.

08:55.460 --> 08:58.930
Anyway, I'm with Chiho 
on the opening shift tomorrow,

08:58.930 --> 09:01.020
so I'll do some casual questioning.

09:02.140 --> 09:05.140
Thank you very much!

09:05.930 --> 09:09.470
Aren't you bein' kinda loud today, Chi?

09:09.470 --> 09:12.900
Hmm? O-Oh, am I? It wasn't on purpose.

09:12.900 --> 09:17.410
Say, wanna go chat 
somewhere after our shift?

09:17.410 --> 09:20.560
Y-You mean on a date?!

09:20.560 --> 09:23.910
Oh, but I'm busy today...

09:23.910 --> 09:25.570
How about tomorrow?

09:25.570 --> 09:29.990
Maybe at a swanky new pasta 
place here in Sasazuka?

09:29.990 --> 09:32.780
There's one of those in Sasazuka?

09:32.780 --> 09:35.670
Oh, but I'm busy tomorrow, too...

09:41.930 --> 09:43.680
You again?

09:43.680 --> 09:46.710
I came to let Alas Ramus 
have some time with the Devil.

09:46.710 --> 09:48.060
Papa!

09:48.060 --> 09:50.330
Chi isn't with you?

09:50.330 --> 09:52.440
We don't hang out <i>every</i> day.

09:52.440 --> 09:56.900
I thought I'd have my girls' 
talk with just Emilia today.

09:57.500 --> 10:00.070
Okay, take care of Alas Ramus.

10:01.560 --> 10:02.480
Ashiya.

10:02.480 --> 10:06.000
Leave it to me, Your Majesty. 
I won't lose them today.

10:06.000 --> 10:06.980
Dumb plan.

10:07.330 --> 10:10.330
How about giving up your old, analog ways?

10:10.330 --> 10:11.090
Huh?

10:14.340 --> 10:16.440
This is going overboard!

10:16.440 --> 10:21.020
I haven't uninstalled the tracker 
I used in Nagano yet, that's all.

10:21.020 --> 10:22.720
Nice work, Urushihara!

10:22.720 --> 10:26.370
Do you finally recognize 
me as more than a moocher?

10:26.370 --> 10:28.200
Moocha!

10:29.980 --> 10:31.270
They stopped.

10:31.270 --> 10:32.730
That's...

10:32.730 --> 10:34.610
<b>Sasa Bath</b>

10:33.220 --> 10:34.610
The bathhouse!

10:36.740 --> 10:42.020
This is the same place I lost 
Emilia and the others before.

10:42.460 --> 10:45.680
It didn't occur to me that 
they'd entered the bathhouse.

10:45.680 --> 10:48.750
Why be so sneaky about going to a bathhouse?

10:49.370 --> 10:53.500
Okay, time to do some Jungle shopping.

10:53.500 --> 10:55.140
Moocha!

10:55.140 --> 11:00.230
Yup, this is mooching. 
I'll mooch a bunch for you, okay?

11:02.010 --> 11:05.850
<b>Sasa Bath</b>

11:06.790 --> 11:08.270
Sire, it's—

11:08.270 --> 11:10.650
Crap, they put up a barrier!

11:12.620 --> 11:14.150
What's up, Urushihara?

11:14.150 --> 11:15.970
<i>We've got trouble, Maou.</i>

11:15.970 --> 11:18.870
It's another video letter from the landlady.

11:21.800 --> 11:23.120
And this time...

11:24.260 --> 11:25.580
instead of a tape...

11:27.670 --> 11:30.900
I never imagined that my first digital video

11:30.900 --> 11:33.020
would be a letter from the landlady.

11:33.020 --> 11:34.880
Should we really do this?

11:41.380 --> 11:42.550
Is that...

11:42.550 --> 11:43.870
...the Amazon?

11:43.870 --> 11:45.390
Why the Amazon?

11:45.390 --> 11:48.640
<i>Good afternoon, Mister Maou and Mister Ashiya.</i>

11:49.380 --> 11:52.180
<i>I apologize that the job I asked you to do</i>

11:52.180 --> 11:58.000
<i>was called off due to my niece's schedule.</i>

11:56.120 --> 11:58.000
What niece?

11:58.000 --> 12:01.700
Ms. Amane. You know, 
from the beach in Choshi.

12:02.150 --> 12:04.070
Oh, yeah.

12:04.070 --> 12:07.110
<i>This may not make up for it,</i>

12:07.110 --> 12:10.200
<i>but would you be so good 
as to weed the back garden?</i>

12:10.200 --> 12:15.170
<i>This will be your payment, 
which I'll deduct from your rent.</i>

12:15.170 --> 12:18.330
<i>Thank you in advance.</i>

12:18.330 --> 12:21.000
I appreciate the ¥15,000, but...

12:21.000 --> 12:24.040
She paused an expedition in the 
deep Amazon to ask for <i>that</i>?

12:24.040 --> 12:27.580
Let's just be glad it was safe to watch.

12:27.580 --> 12:29.810
Weeding, huh?

12:31.060 --> 12:33.810
Gentlemen, we can use this!

12:42.070 --> 12:46.210
You sure doing this in 
the blazing sun isn't deadly?

12:46.210 --> 12:49.330
I'll admit it's harder labor than I thought.

12:49.330 --> 12:52.120
Sorry to make you help us, Chi.

12:52.120 --> 12:56.210
It's fine. I'm the one who offered.

12:56.210 --> 12:57.580
Thank you, too, Suzuno.

12:57.580 --> 13:00.410
Everyone should work to 
keep their environs tidy.

13:00.410 --> 13:01.930
Papa!

13:04.170 --> 13:06.260
Hi, Alas Ramus!

13:06.260 --> 13:07.870
Hello, Miss Yusa!

13:07.870 --> 13:10.810
What are you all doing? 
And with Chiho and Bel, too?

13:10.810 --> 13:13.720
Isn't it obvious? We're weeding!

13:13.720 --> 13:15.810
We finished at the perfect time.

13:15.810 --> 13:17.770
Shall we go, then?

13:17.770 --> 13:19.610
Come on, guys, we'll go too.

13:19.610 --> 13:21.750
Go where?

13:21.750 --> 13:24.580
Just to the bathhouse. We're all sweaty.

13:28.320 --> 13:30.930
Wow, you were planning a bath, too?

13:30.930 --> 13:33.250
My goodness, what a coincidence!

13:33.250 --> 13:34.770
Should we skip today?

13:34.770 --> 13:39.430
It doesn't matter. We can't 
keep them in the dark forever.

13:39.430 --> 13:40.950
What're you talking about?

13:40.950 --> 13:42.960
N-N-Nothing.

13:42.960 --> 13:45.640
Papa, Mama, bath together!

13:45.640 --> 13:50.640
L-Listen, Alas Ramus, Papa 
and Mama can't bathe together.

13:53.210 --> 13:54.650
Three people.

13:54.650 --> 13:55.850
Okay.

13:55.850 --> 13:58.480
Papa too!

13:58.480 --> 14:01.480
No, honey, Papa can't come with us.

14:01.840 --> 14:03.140
Maou.

14:03.140 --> 14:04.780
Yes, Ms. Toyo?

14:04.780 --> 14:06.110
That your wife?

14:06.670 --> 14:09.110
She's the mother, but not my wife.

14:12.260 --> 14:14.120
We got here first again today.

14:14.480 --> 14:17.130
All right, let's start training.

14:17.130 --> 14:18.870
Train!

14:18.870 --> 14:21.750
Yes, please!

14:22.340 --> 14:23.540
Training?

14:23.540 --> 14:25.630
Training for what?

14:34.510 --> 14:36.560
First, drink this.

14:36.560 --> 14:37.720
Right.

14:39.020 --> 14:41.010
What is she drinking?

14:41.760 --> 14:43.560
Could it be coffee milk?

14:43.560 --> 14:45.840
Drinking that in the bath is bad manners!

14:45.840 --> 14:47.650
<i>That's</i> your issue here?

14:47.650 --> 14:51.270
What kind of training can they do 
with coffee milk, though?

14:51.270 --> 14:52.200
MgCafé?!

14:52.200 --> 14:53.790
Where did that come from?

14:57.010 --> 14:58.310
But...

14:58.310 --> 15:00.090
Every time I see them...

15:01.100 --> 15:05.150
How are we so different? I know 
my nutrition is at least as good.

15:05.150 --> 15:09.150
Th-Think about it, though, Bel! 
They'd be a nuisance in battle!

15:09.150 --> 15:12.430
T-True. Different rules for noncombatants.

15:12.430 --> 15:14.120
Noncombatants?

15:14.120 --> 15:15.590
A nuisance in battle?

15:15.590 --> 15:17.170
What's going on?

15:20.050 --> 15:21.560
Is something wrong?

15:21.560 --> 15:23.770
Look in a mirror.

15:23.770 --> 15:24.940
Huh?

15:25.620 --> 15:28.180
It's nothing. Forget it.

15:30.310 --> 15:34.750
Your vital signs seem stable. 
Any changes in your condition?

15:34.750 --> 15:35.700
Nope!

15:35.700 --> 15:39.260
Don't be nervous. 
Relax, like your normal self.

15:39.260 --> 15:41.630
That's what the bathhouse setting is for.

15:41.630 --> 15:44.890
Let's begin. First, waterfall training.

15:44.890 --> 15:46.710
Wadderfall!

15:46.710 --> 15:49.210
Waterfall training for a MgCafé job?!

15:49.210 --> 15:51.800
I'm telling you, it's not about MgCafé.

15:51.800 --> 15:55.070
How would they even do that in a bathhouse?

15:55.720 --> 15:57.970
Look, Sire.

15:57.970 --> 15:59.370
With those!

16:09.860 --> 16:12.960
All right, that's probably enough.

16:12.960 --> 16:15.270
Next, get in the lukewarm bath.

16:15.270 --> 16:15.990
Right!

16:18.490 --> 16:22.130
Good. This way you can 
really focus on your head

16:22.130 --> 16:24.960
where the shower water fell, right?

16:24.960 --> 16:28.460
Now imagine celestial force flowing 
from there throughout your body,

16:28.460 --> 16:30.010
down to the tips of your toes.

16:35.010 --> 16:39.260
Good, you're doing well. 
Now open your eyes and sit up.

16:39.730 --> 16:42.520
Now I do the other thing, right?

16:42.870 --> 16:44.120
That's right.

16:44.120 --> 16:47.390
Essentially, our techniques are 
about giving form to what we imagine.

16:47.390 --> 16:51.330
Still, the concept of activating 
celestial force is difficult to imagine.

16:51.330 --> 16:52.980
Thus, we vocalize.

16:52.980 --> 16:57.370
Like how I say "Divine Boots of Light" 
or Bel says "Light of Iron."

16:57.370 --> 17:00.040
Saying things aloud 
makes your image of them concrete.

17:00.040 --> 17:03.270
Celestial force? Light of Iron?

17:03.270 --> 17:05.560
This is a bathhouse! What are they doing?

17:05.560 --> 17:07.810
Making a bloodbath? It <i>is</i> a bathhouse.

17:07.810 --> 17:09.020
I'm gonna take a look.

17:09.020 --> 17:14.260
Stop, Sire! If you enter the women's 
bath naked, the police will be called!

17:14.980 --> 17:17.430
They'll call the cops 
whether he's naked or not.

17:17.430 --> 17:18.320
Let me go, Ashiya!

17:18.990 --> 17:24.460
Fear not, good Chiho. They can't do 
anything while we're in the women's bath.

17:24.460 --> 17:26.460
There's a force field up,

17:26.460 --> 17:30.370
and I'll put the front desk lady 
to sleep again. Don't worry.

17:31.770 --> 17:33.550
Now shout, good Chiho.

17:33.960 --> 17:39.020
You're only practicing activating 
celestial force, so any words will do.

17:39.020 --> 17:40.950
Just shout as loud as you can.

17:40.950 --> 17:43.930
B-But if Mister Maou hears me...

17:43.930 --> 17:49.680
Overcoming turmoil and humiliation greatly 
intensifies the psychological release.

17:49.680 --> 17:53.710
This should be even more effective 
with Maou on the other side of the wall.

18:01.730 --> 18:02.940
Chi?!

18:02.940 --> 18:05.320
Please come to your senses, Sire!

18:05.320 --> 18:08.230
If you get caught, you'll be
branded a pervert for life!

18:08.830 --> 18:11.450
Fine! Then we'll have Urushihara do it!

18:11.450 --> 18:14.980
Don't talk like it doesn't matter 
if I'm branded a pervert!

18:16.740 --> 18:18.990
Use your diaphragm!

18:20.890 --> 18:22.830
That's the spirit!

18:22.830 --> 18:24.010
Pipe down!

18:24.010 --> 18:25.500
Papa!

18:25.500 --> 18:28.240
Don't shout with them, Alas Ramus!

18:29.550 --> 18:32.360
Hey, Emi! I don't know 
what you're doing in there,

18:32.360 --> 18:33.950
but yelling is rude, so make them stop!

18:33.950 --> 18:36.570
I'll explain later, so just ignore it for now!

18:36.570 --> 18:38.330
Come have a drink!

18:38.330 --> 18:40.820
I'd love to!

18:39.460 --> 18:40.820
Izakaya roleplay?!

18:40.820 --> 18:43.150
Damn it, I don't even care if I get arrested!

18:40.820 --> 18:43.510
Papa!

18:43.510 --> 18:45.010
King Satan!

18:50.270 --> 18:51.440
Emi!

18:51.770 --> 18:54.400
What are you doing to Chi?

18:54.400 --> 18:56.010
You can't tell?

18:56.610 --> 18:59.160
Well, I suppose we didn't use much.

18:59.840 --> 19:00.760
Huh?

19:00.760 --> 19:02.940
Seriously, what are you thinking?

19:02.940 --> 19:07.110
Are you trying to shoot yourself 
in the foot, wasting frontline forces

19:07.110 --> 19:09.040
on protecting a soldier who can't fight?

19:09.040 --> 19:11.220
Of course not.

19:11.600 --> 19:13.620
And she understands perfectly.

19:13.620 --> 19:17.400
But she says she wants the power 
to warn you or one of us

19:17.400 --> 19:19.800
if there's an emergency situation.

19:19.800 --> 19:22.330
Warn us? Do you mean...?

19:22.330 --> 19:24.300
Yes. Idea linking.

19:25.360 --> 19:29.980
Sariel took her phone when 
he kidnapped her, remember?

19:29.980 --> 19:31.100
So yeah.

19:31.810 --> 19:33.320
Chi...

19:33.320 --> 19:36.560
I'm pretty sure all she wants is to 
make sure that if she's in a crisis,

19:36.560 --> 19:40.570
she doesn't cause you more 
trouble than necessary.

19:41.220 --> 19:46.230
The good Chiho put a lot of thought 
into this course of action.

19:46.230 --> 19:47.330
Suzu-sis!

19:47.330 --> 19:49.700
Please respect her feelings.

19:50.210 --> 19:53.080
M-Mr. Maou...

19:53.080 --> 19:54.560
Chi...

19:54.560 --> 19:57.230
Don't come crying to me 
when this goes wrong.

19:57.230 --> 19:59.460
Miss Sasaki, did you...?

20:02.320 --> 20:08.970
I don't want to get in your way 
or drag you down.

20:09.960 --> 20:16.830
I need to make sure I can always 
escape, or help you help me...

20:16.830 --> 20:18.230
Chi-sis!

20:18.920 --> 20:24.570
Jeez, don't worry about that. 
We're monsters from another world, you know.

20:24.570 --> 20:27.190
You can leave all the responsibility to us.

20:27.190 --> 20:29.120
We're the ones who got you mixed up in this.

20:29.120 --> 20:32.050
You know Chiho's not 
the kind of person to do that.

20:32.050 --> 20:34.340
I can't think of anything more touching

20:34.340 --> 20:38.130
than someone wanting power 
not to leap into danger,

20:38.680 --> 20:40.850
but to escape or help her rescuers.

20:43.470 --> 20:46.140
Thank you so much for today.

20:46.510 --> 20:49.140
No problem. Next is practical experience.

20:49.580 --> 20:50.630
Um...

20:51.450 --> 20:57.390
There's something I think I need to report 
to you... or, well, talk to you about.

20:57.390 --> 20:59.900
What's with the vague phrasing?

20:59.900 --> 21:04.400
After whoever that was entered my body,

21:04.400 --> 21:07.030
they left extra memories behind.

21:08.410 --> 21:11.230
I can see a large man.

21:11.230 --> 21:14.380
He's got a beard, and his hair is tied back.

21:14.380 --> 21:16.150
A middle-aged man who seems nice.

21:16.150 --> 21:18.670
He's standing in a golden field of rice...

21:20.170 --> 21:24.040
Any chance that was wheat and not rice?

21:24.420 --> 21:26.180
Maybe so.

21:26.180 --> 21:32.680
And then he says a word: "aciethalla."

21:33.120 --> 21:35.180
"Aciethalla"?

21:35.180 --> 21:37.560
Do you know what it means?

21:37.560 --> 21:39.780
No, I don't.

21:40.330 --> 21:41.440
But...

21:43.420 --> 21:49.950
If you have a memory of that man, 
the person inside you must have been...

21:53.510 --> 21:56.270
What's wrong, Sire?

21:56.270 --> 21:57.560
Nothing.

21:58.850 --> 22:00.950
This was the correct decision, right?

22:28.780 --> 22:30.870
<b>The Devil is a Part-Timer! Season 2</b>
